# Popup design (AsanPay)

Every new popup must look like the Linked accounts "Verify account" popup. Never ship a bare title + X box.

## Use the shared shell — don't hand-roll

| Surface | Component |
|---|---|
| Agent web | `apps/agent-portal/components/ui/Modal.tsx` (`icon`, `iconTone`, `eyebrow`, `subtitle`, `wide`) |
| Admin web | `apps/admin-portal/components/ui/Modal.tsx` (same props, dark-mode safe) |
| Confirm / delete | `ConfirmModal` (agent) · `DangerConfirmModal` (admin) |
| Mobile | `components/ModalSheet.tsx` — **centered** popup (not a bottom sheet), same props (`icon`, `iconTone`, `eyebrow`, `subtitle`); body scrolls so footer buttons always show. `scroll={false}` only when the body has its own FlatList. `PulseIcon` lives in `components/PulseIcon.tsx`. |

## Required anatomy

1. **Icon tile** left of the title: 48 px, rounded-2xl, soft tone background, **pulse animation** (`confirm-modal-icon` agent / `modal-icon-pulse` admin / `PulseIcon` mobile). Pick an icon that names the action (Send, Undo2, Wallet, UserPlus, ShieldCheck, History…).
2. **Tone = intent**: blue info / submit · green success / add · amber reverse / warning · red danger / failed check.
3. **Eyebrow** (optional, `Step 2 of 2`) → **Title** (text-xl) → **Subtitle** (one line: what to check / what happens).
4. **Body** in cards (rounded-2xl, light border, `#F7F9FF` gradient for the main card). Related facts as small label/value tiles, not long one-column tables.
5. **Wide content** (> ~6 rows) → `wide` + `sm:grid-cols-2`; must stack to one column below `sm`. Balance column heights — no empty blank area inside a card (use `h-full flex-col` + a bottom summary / helper strip with `mt-auto`).
6. **Status lists** (checks, steps): row per item with icon + label + status pill; stagger in with `la-check-row` (`animationDelay` 120 ms steps) and end with a summary strip (green all good / red what failed).
7. **Inputs**: full-width fields like the mobile number field (not digit boxes) unless the design explicitly shows boxes; group related inputs in a `B.bg` panel, side by side on `sm+`.
8. **Close (✕)**: always the red tile — web `className="popup-close"` (light red, fills red + rotates on hover), mobile `<PopupCloseButton />`. Never a plain grey ✕.
9. **Footer**: two equal buttons per `button-color-semantics` (Back = secondary, Cancel = red, Submit = blue, Add/Link = green). Disabled until valid.
10. **Motion**: panel pop-in (`confirm-modal-panel`), backdrop blur; respect `prefers-reduced-motion` / `AccessibilityInfo.isReduceMotionEnabled()`.
11. **Copy**: English only, field-specific errors inline (`clear-error-messages`), never show another person's data in a failed check.

## Parity

Same popup on web and mobile in the same change (`web-mobile-parity`). Mobile may stack instead of two columns — note it as a platform exception. No bottom-sheet popups on mobile; never put a ScrollView inside `ModalSheet` (it already scrolls).

## When touching an old popup

If it still uses a plain title + X layout, upgrade it to this anatomy in the same change (at minimum: icon tile + tone + subtitle).
